  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Securing a future for Grauer&apos;s gorilla and eastern chimpanzees in the Kasese region of Democratic Republic of Congo</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this 1-year project is to extend the effective protection of Grauers gorilla habitat to 60% of its range. Specific activities include: 1) extending protection for Grauers gorillas from the Kahuzi-Biega National Park to neighboring areas through supporting the legalization of the adjacent Oku Community Reserve; 2) improving the governance structures of the proposed community reserve; and 3) increasing the national conservation authority&apos;s ability to counter armed poaching and security threats through the development of a rapid reaction unit.</narrative>
  </description>
